function infoCc_injectToCodex()
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addCategory', 'cc_cat', 'Cosmic Chronicles'%_t, 'data/textures/icons/trading.png')

    -- Full Feature Breakdown
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'cc_cat', 'cc_cat_c0', 'Full Feature Breakdown'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a0', 'The Rumormonger System'%_t, 'Adds dynamic background chatter and interactive rumor-gathering to all NPC stations in the game. Features a rapidly expanding registry of over 60+ unique, localized lore strings.\n\nKey Mechanics:\n\n- Ambient Chatter: Stations run a background chatter loop on a 45-second per-sector cooldown, broadcasting floating overhead text based on their specific type and current situation once that cooldown lapses.\n- Interaction: Players can dock and access a direct dialogue menu to ask \"Any rumors?\" and receive a dynamic tip.\n- Tutorialization: The Rumormonger now acts as an immersive guide, occasionally broadcasting tips to teach players about complex mechanics (e.g., Merchant synergies, Trash Man filters) naturally through gameplay.\n- Contextual Awareness: The Rumormonger actively parses and adapts to:\n  - Station Type: Dynamically identifies 12 vanilla station scripts (shipyards, repair docks, equipment docks, military outposts, smugglers markets, casinos, and more), caching the result on the station the first time it\'s checked.\n  - War Heat: Pulls live conflict data from the Cosmic War bridge.\n  - Faction Wealth: Differentiates between wealthy and poor economies.\n  - Geography: Certain rumors (like Deep Core lore) will not spawn near the Outer Rim.\n  - Player Reputation: Station inhabitants refuse to gossip with outlaws (cuts off at -30,000 rep for everyone, regardless of captain), preventing hostile military outposts from offering out-of-character dialogue.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a1', 'Captains Logs'%_t, 'Hooks directly into the Cosmic Overhaul background command simulation.\n\nKey Mechanics:\n\n- When a captain completes a map command (Scout, Mine, Trade, etc.) and sends the player a mail report, a narrative "Captain\'s Log" is dynamically appended to the bottom of the message.\n- Context Validation: Logs react directly to the parent faction and sector data where the operation took place. For example, trading in a high War Heat sector triggers logs detailing aggressive military patrols or close calls with blockades.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a2', 'Dynamic Narrative Events'%_t, 'A global event controller listens for hyperspace jumps and spawns immersive, world-building events based on the local geopolitical climate.\n\nAvailable Events:\n\n1. Refugee Convoys: Spawns off live Cosmic War humanitarian/retreat reports rather than a fixed heat number — a nearby report has roughly a 30% chance (governed by a per-region cooldown) of manifesting as a convoy. Fleeing civilian ships appear with damaged hyperdrives. Players can donate Food or Medical Supplies to rescue them for reputation and rumors, with a 25% chance the refugees tip off the exact coordinates of a hidden resource stash.\n   - Captain Synergy: Merchants negotiate Hazard Pay; Smugglers can skim supplies for massive credit payouts.\n2. Echoes of the Frontline (Graveyards): Same news-driven system, keyed off Cosmic War battle/aftermath/siege reports instead (roughly a 35% chance, same per-region cooldown). Players may stumble upon massive wreckage fields—the immediate aftermath of a fleet clash.\n3. Black Box Extraction: Players can interact with Stashes in Graveyards to extract audio logs, System Upgrades and credits.\n   - Captain Synergy: Scavengers extract 50% more value (1.5x); Explorers extract 25% more (1.25x) and can reach a Black Box from further away. Better rolls raise the odds of an Uncommon upgrade climbing to Rare or even Legendary.\n4. Cinematic Monuments: (Deep inside AI territory). Spawns colossal procedural monuments. Reading the inscription grants a permanent +2500 reputation boost.\n5. Drifting Ghost Ship: Intercept a faint distress signal from a derelict freighter and trigger a narrative dialog.\n6. Rogue AI Probe: Spawns a fast, evasive military probe whose fire rate alone climbs the closer you engage it to the galactic core — no bonus out at the sector edge, scaling smoothly up to 5x right at the Core. Shields and other stats aren\'t touched. Destroy it before it escapes with scanned data.\n7. Stranded Diplomat: A faction\'s diplomat is stranded in hostile space. Extract them before capture.\n8. Ancient Data Caches: Derelict data banks that yield Encrypted Log Fragments. Trade these fragments at any Research Station for credit and reputation rewards.\n9. Ancient Eclipse Anomaly: Intercept strange energy readings pointing to a volatile, physical anomaly. Navigate carefully and extract its core to receive rare System Upgrades before it destabilizes and detonates.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a3', 'Synergy Updates'%_t, '- Corrupted Lore Nodes: Data caches in Eclipse territory offer 2x rewards but instantly spawn a massive Ascendancy ambush.\n- Explorer Resonance: Ships commanded by an Explorer captain gain a 3x (500 to 1,500) interaction range on Black Boxes.\n- Galactic Lore Broadcasts: Finding a Legendary subsystem or massive credits in a data cache broadcasts your discovery globally via Cosmic Vault News.\n- Famine Relief Anomalies: Interact with emergency relief caches during severe faction famines to either steal the loot or donate it for massive reputation (+25,000) and instant famine reduction.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a4', 'Rift DLC Interoperability'%_t, '- Classified Rift Tech: Recovered Black Boxes now have a chance to drop highly-classified Rift Research Data and Subclass Subsystems. These contraband goods are extremely valuable on the black market.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a5', 'Cosmic Vault Synergy'%_t, '- Unified News API: Verified reports from Cosmic War, Cosmic Overhaul, Cosmic Ascendancy, and Vault itself all surface in the same Galactic News feed, routed through Vault\'s shared News architecture for validation and persistence.\n- Shared Dialogue Context: The Rumormonger doesn\'t just react to its own state — its lines are chosen using live faction wealth, war heat, weather, and Rift activity pulled straight from Vault\'s shared data, so a station\'s mood always matches what\'s actually happening in the galaxy around it.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a6', 'Network Safety & Anti-Cheat'%_t, '- Math.Random Fix: Unstable Lua math.random calls are replaced with Avorion\'s deterministic random():getInt() sequence. This guarantees 100% synchronization on Multiplayer Dedicated Servers and prevents cascading desyncs.\n- Callable Validation: UI and background scripts have been fully hardened. Malicious clients can no longer spoof "free" remote calls; the server actively verifies execution contexts before processing any requests, sealing Arbitrary Code Execution (ACE) vulnerabilities.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a8', 'Galactic News & Economy'%_t, 'Cosmic Chronicles adds a living news network to the galaxy.\n\nKey Features:\n\n- Galactic News Network: Real-time broadcasts of verified sector events pulled from Cosmic War, Cosmic Overhaul, Cosmic Ascendancy, and Vault itself — battles, sieges, factory reports, weather, and Rift activity all surface here.\n- Ambient Economic Flavor: Station chatter and rumors reference shortages, blockades, and other local color reacting to a sector\'s situation — atmosphere, not a mechanic that physically alters trading profits.\n- Deep Space Discoveries: Find massive, bespoke monoliths, data caches, and lore fragments hidden in uncharted sectors.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cc_cat_c0', 'cc_cat_a9', 'The Vanilla Way vs The Cosmic Way'%_t, 'Vanilla Avorion features "Radio Chatter", which randomly prints static strings over station models without any context.\n\nThe Cosmic Way: The Rumormonger system completely overrides this. Every piece of dialogue you see floating above a station, or spoken to you in the docking menu, is dynamically built. It considers the station type, the local economy, the faction\'s current war heat, and your specific captain\'s subclass before choosing what to say.\n'%_t, '')
end
